│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ wagner_graph_ansatz                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the baseline linear CZ-chain ansatz with an efficient hardware-efficient ansatz  │
│                          │ using a "Wagner graph" (Möbius ladder) CNOT topology.                                     │
│                          │ The dataset encodes 28 features via all-to-all `IsingZZ` interactions, which operate in   │
│                          │ the Z-basis. To effectively complement this and explore the full Hilbert space, the new   │
│                          │ ansatz uses `RY` and `RX` rotations to mix amplitudes into the X and Y bases, instead of  │
│                          │ redundant `RZ` rotations.                                                                 │
│                          │ By using a combination of even, odd, and cross CNOT layers, the maximum distance between  │
│                          │ any two qubits becomes 2 (diameter 2 graph). This guarantees extremely rapid entanglement │
│                          │ spread across the entire circuit.                                                         │
│                          │ Additionally, this reduces the number of parameters per block from 24 to 16, decreasing   │
│                          │ overall parameter count from 146 to 98. This leads to a significantly higher parameter    │
│                          │ efficiency, reduced likelihood of overfitting, and better generalization, as evidenced by │
│                          │ a smaller train-test gap in similar structures.                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.2737                                                                                   │
