│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_cube_mixer                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The fixed trainer uses three data uploads, two independently parameterized ansatz blocks  │
│                          │ per upload, Adam with a default learning rate of 0.03, 30 minibatch steps per epoch,      │
│                          │ batch size 15, a 0.90 convergence threshold, and validation-loss early stopping with      │
│                          │ patience 75 and minimum delta 1e-4.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The seed has 24 unique parameters per block and 146 total parameters. Its line of CZ      │
│                          │ gates treats endpoint qubits differently, while the terminal RZ layer cannot directly     │
│                          │ affect the final Z readout. The proposed block instead uses four shared parameters per    │
│                          │ block, reducing the total to 26. Collective rotations impose a useful graph-like symmetry │
│                          │ prior and reduce overfitting, while independent parameter copies across the six blocks    │
│                          │ preserve data-reuploading flexibility. A regular 3-dimensional cube entangler connects    │
│                          │ every qubit with equal degree using three parallel perfect matchings, avoiding the        │
│                          │ endpoint bias and serial depth of the CZ line. The final RY/RX layers convert both phase  │
│                          │ quadratures generated by IsingZZ encoding into measurable Z populations. This             │
│                          │ configuration should improve parameter efficiency, reduce the generalization gap, and     │
│                          │ provide stronger gradients with lower circuit depth.                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
