╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hypercube_ry_cascade                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz uses a 3-dimensional hypercube entangling topology instead of a linear chain. │
│                          │ For 8 qubits (labeled as 3-bit binary strings 000-111), the hypercube connects qubit      │
│                          │ pairs that differ in exactly one bit, organized into 3 parallel layers:                   │
│                          │ - Dim 0: (0,1),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7) — pairs differing in bit 0                               │
│                          │ - Dim 1: (0,2),(1,3),(4,6),(5,7) — pairs differing in bit 1                               │
│                          │ - Dim 2: (0,4),(1,5),(2,6),(3,7) — pairs differing in bit 2                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This ensures every qubit pair is connected by at most log2(8)=3 CZ gates — optimal        │
│                          │ diameter. Between each entangling layer, RY rotations convert accumulated phases into     │
│                          │ amplitude differences observable in Z measurements. A final RZ layer provides phase       │
│                          │ tuning. This replaces the seed's linear CZ chain (diameter 7) with a log-depth structure  │
│                          │ that propagates correlations exponentially faster, critical for the IsingZZ-encoded       │
│                          │ features which create qubit-pair correlations across the full register. The RY-dominated  │
│                          │ rotation basis is specifically chosen because RY gates are the only real single-qubit     │
│                          │ rotations that don't commute with Z, making them maximally effective at extracting phase  │
│                          │ information into Z-measurement outcomes.                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.1782                                                                                   │
