│ patch_name               │ telescoping_entangler                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This ansatz introduces a "telescoping" multi-scale approach to quantum entanglement,      │
│                          │ acting across three different spatial topologies within the 8-qubit register. It draws    │
│                          │ inspiration from strongly entangling layers but replaces uniform connectivity with a      │
│                          │ nested structure.                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. It begins with dense single-qubit local preparations (RY, RZ).                         │
│                          │ 2. It applies a nearest-neighbor ring of CZ gates for tight local entanglement (stride    │
│                          │ 1).                                                                                       │
│                          │ 3. After intermediate local RX rotations to tilt the Bloch vector, it applies long-range  │
│                          │ CNOT gates (stride 4) to instantly share information between the two distant halves of    │
│                          │ the register.                                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Medium-range CRY parameterized entangling gates (stride 2) follow, smoothly            │
│                          │ fine-tuning the interactions and increasing expressivity.                                 │
│                          │ 5. An output layer of independent RY gates correctly adjusts the axis prior to the        │
│                          │ subsequent data uploading or final Z-measurements.                                        │
│                          │ By mixing rigid unparameterized topological gates (CZ, CNOT) with parameterized ones      │
│                          │ (CRY) across multiple distances, this architecture significantly boosts expressiveness    │
│                          │ while maintaining strong gradient flows for the Adam optimizer.                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
