│ patch_description        │ Replace the redundant all-to-all CZ layer with a degree-three Möbius-ladder graph         │
│                          │ organized into three disjoint perfect matchings: alternating ring edges, shifted ring     │
│                          │ edges, and opposite-node chords. This preserves uniform qubit connectivity and matches    │
│                          │ the collective rotations and mean-Z readout while reducing each block from 28 to 12       │
│                          │ entanglers. The total gate count falls from 396 to 300 without changing the 20 trainable  │
│                          │ parameters. Grouping disjoint edges also substantially lowers depth, while repeated       │
│                          │ uploads and blocks retain sufficient propagation capacity. The sparser symmetric graph    │
│                          │ should regularize the model, maintain the small train-test gap, and improve the           │
│                          │ complexity-adjusted combined score.                                                       │
