│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ orbit_twist                                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This design retains the parameter-efficient collective rotations that generalized well in │
│                          │ the current program, but replaces the sparse cube entangler with an exact                 │
│                          │ permutation-equivariant interaction. Every pair of qubits receives one CZ, producing a    │
│                          │ complete-graph quadratic phase—or collective one-axis twist—between noncommuting mixer    │
│                          │ layers.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Because the 28 encoded features correspond to two-qubit relationships, treating all qubit │
│                          │ pairs identically removes the arbitrary reference graph introduced by the cube. The       │
│                          │ resulting hypothesis class is aligned with vertex-permutation-invariant record            │
│                          │ properties, which should reduce nuisance fitting and improve validation behavior. The 28  │
│                          │ CZ gates are ordered as seven disjoint perfect matchings, giving the complete interaction │
│                          │ layer its minimum possible two-qubit depth on eight qubits. Parameter sharing preserves   │
│                          │ the current total of only four circuit parameters per block, while the collective RY/RZ   │
│                          │ and RY/RX stages provide phase injection and phase-to-population conversion for the fixed │
│                          │ Z readout.                                                                                │
