│ patch_name               │ collective_complete_graph_mixer                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the overparameterized wire-specific block with a permutation-equivariant          │
│                          │ four-parameter block. Shared rotations align with the symmetric mean-Z readout and should │
│                          │ reduce the observed train-validation gap, while the complete CZ graph matches the 28      │
│                          │ possible feature-pair channels and previously produced substantially stronger validation  │
│                          │ accuracy than sparse connectivity. A new shared RX layer directly after the collective RY │
│                          │ layer provides two-axis input mixing, and the final collective RZ-RX pair keeps the last  │
│                          │ operation non-diagonal so it can directly affect Z readout. This reduces the model from   │
│                          │ 194 to 26 total parameters while retaining expressive all-to-all interactions.            │
