│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ k44_bipartite_entangler                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This approach replaces the full K8 complete graph of CZ gates with a K4,4 bipartite graph │
│                          │ entangler. We partition the 8 qubits into two sets of 4 and connect them using four       │
│                          │ perfect matchings. This reduces the number of two-qubit gates per block from 28 to 16,    │
│                          │ significantly lowering the circuit depth and overall gate count, while still maintaining  │
│                          │ high connectivity and expressive power. The parameter count remains at a highly efficient │
│                          │ 3 parameters per block, utilizing collective RY, RZ, and RX rotations to maintain         │
│                          │ permutation symmetry and aggregate gradients effectively. This lower depth is expected to │
│                          │ improve parameter efficiency and execution speed without sacrificing training or          │
│                          │ generalization performance.                                                               │
