                         Patch Metadata - Gen 18/50 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ five_param_ry_mid_enhanced                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ This design extends the proven best ansatz (score 0.98) with one additional collective    │
│                          │ rotation layer. The structure is:                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. RY(collective) + RX(collective_in): Two-axis input mixer that prepares states in a     │
│                          │ rich subspace for entanglement                                                            │
│                          │ 2. CZ complete graph (28 pairs): All-to-all entanglement matching the feature pair        │
│                          │ connectivity                                                                              │
│                          │ 3. RY(collective_mid): NEW - Post-entanglement rotation that allows the circuit to        │
│                          │ process entangled states before output transformation                                     │
│                          │ 4. RZ(collective) + RX(collective_out): Two-axis output mixer that converts entangled     │
│                          │ phase correlations into the Z-measurement basis                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ After CZ creates correlations in the Z basis, RY_mid rotates the entangled states into    │
│                          │ positions where the subsequent RZ+RX output layers can extract richer information. This   │
│                          │ adds only 1 parameter per block (5 total vs 4) while significantly expanding the          │
│                          │ circuit's expressivity. All parameters remain collective (shared across qubits) for       │
