│ patch_name               │ two_axis_input_plus_mid_mixer                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz only has a single-axis (RY) input mixer, whereas the best-performing   │
│                          │ prior (0.98) uses two axes (RY+RX). Additionally, all 28 CZ gates commute and effectively │
│                          │ form a single diagonal unitary regardless of ordering. By splitting the CZ block into two │
│                          │ halves and inserting a collective two-axis mixer (RY+RX) between them, we break this      │
│                          │ commutativity, creating a much richer unitary that can capture more complex feature       │
│                          │ interactions. This adds only 2 shared parameters (mid_ry, mid_rx) beyond the proven       │
│                          │ 4-parameter structure, totaling 6 params per block (38 total). The increased expressivity │
│                          │ should push validation accuracy higher and reduce loss, outweighing any parameter         │
│                          │ efficiency penalty.                                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
