│                          │ test accuracy of 0.96. The current program replaced the naive 28-depth CZ sequence with   │
│                          │ an optimal 7-depth one-factorization schedule, but dropped the extra rotation layers,     │
│                          │ resulting in lower test accuracy (0.95) and score (0.78).                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Since all CZ gates commute, changing their application order does not alter the           │
│                          │ mathematical unitary of the ansatz block. By combining the optimal 7-depth CZ scheduling  │
│                          │ of the current program with the expressive two-axis input and output rotation layers of   │
│                          │ the best previous program, we will mathematically recreate the exact same training        │
│                          │ trajectory and high accuracy (0.96) of the 0.98-scoring program, but with a more          │
│                          │ hardware-efficient circuit depth.                                                         │
