│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the rigid `CZ` interactions with parameterized `CRZ` gates, leveraging │
│                          │ the existing one-factorization of the K8 complete graph (7 perfect matchings). Each       │
│                          │ matching is assigned a shared parameter, `crz_match_0` through `crz_match_6`. This        │
│                          │ provides tunable entanglement strength per matching, which is a powerful enhancement when │
│                          │ working with highly symmetric and parallelizable topologies.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, this change restores the two-axis input and output collective mixers (`RY`  │
│                          │ + `RX` for input, and `RZ` + `RX` for output) that yielded exceptional test accuracy      │
│                          │ (~0.98) in earlier iterations, effectively balancing expressivity and                     │
│                          │ parameter-efficiency.                                                                     │
