│ patch_description        │ The previous iteration severely underparameterized the single-qubit mixers by using only  │
│                          │ `RY` at the input and `RX` at the output (2 parameters per block). This lacked sufficient │
│                          │ expressivity to fully rotate the qubits into the optimal bases between the dense          │
│                          │ complete-graph entangling layers, dropping the combined score to 0.78.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By restoring a 4-parameter symmetric mixer (`RY_in`, `RX_in` at the input and `RZ_out`,   │
│                          │ `RX_out` at the output), we provide complete control over the single-qubit basis          │
│                          │ transformations. These four collective rotations perfectly maintain the circuit's         │
│                          │ permutation equivariance while giving the Adam optimizer enough flexibility to navigate   │
│                          │ the loss landscape efficiently, closing the train-test gap and reliably reaching >0.95    │
│                          │ combined score.                                                                           │
