│ patch_name               │ sparse_ring_ansatz                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replaces the dense complete-graph K8 entangling layer with a sparse 1D ring (cycle) of CZ │
│                          │ gates. Since the fixed data-encoding feature map already provides dense all-to-all phase  │
│                          │ entanglement (via 28 IsingZZ couplings per upload), the ansatz block only needs minimal   │
│                          │ topological connectivity to propagate these phases into observable amplitude differences. │
│                          │ The sparse ring topology drastically reduces the gate count and circuit depth, improving  │
│                          │ parameter efficiency and reducing optimization difficulty (mitigating the barren plateau  │
│                          │ effect) while maintaining full permutation-symmetric expressive power through shared      │
│                          │ collective single-qubit rotations.                                                        │
