│ patch_description        │ The fixed optimizer uses Adam with learning rate 0.03, batches of 15, 30 steps per epoch, │
│                          │ validation-loss early stopping, three uploads, and two independently parameterized ansatz │
│                          │ repeats per upload. The current block has four shared parameters but places all 28        │
│                          │ commuting CZ gates together, limiting nonlinear processing and converging only after      │
│                          │ about 270 steps.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed block retains the complete K8 interaction graph but partitions it into three │
│                          │ balanced, dihedrally regular edge groups. Collective RY and RX mixers are inserted        │
│                          │ between these groups, so uploaded phases are repeatedly converted into populations before │
│                          │ subsequent interactions. All rotations remain shared across eight wires, yielding only    │
│                          │ six parameters per block and 38 total parameters including readout. This matches the      │
│                          │ parameter count and gate count of the strongest prior architecture while distributing its │
│                          │ middle mixer across two entangling stages for greater effective depth and improved        │
│                          │ gradient flow.                                                                            │
