│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_cz_mid_mixer_one_factorization                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replicate the structure of the best-performing prior (score 1.07) which uses:             │
│                          │ 1. Two-axis non-commuting input mixer (RY + RX)                                           │
│                          │ 2. Complete-graph CZ split into two halves with a mid-circuit RY+RX mixer between them    │
│                          │ 3. Two-axis output mixer (RZ + RX)                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The mid-mixer breaks the commutativity of the CZ layers, dramatically increasing          │
│                          │ expressivity. The CZ gates use the one-factorization of K8 for optimal parallel depth.    │
│                          │ This gives 6 shared params per block × 6 blocks = 36 circuit + 2 readout = 38 total       │
│                          │ params, matching the best prior.                                                          │
