│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ interleaved_complete_graph_ansatz                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The previous best architecture achieved higher generalization and accuracy by inserting a │
│                          │ mid-circuit mixer to break up the 28 commuting CZ gates, allowing the circuit to process  │
│                          │ the phases introduced by the initial entangling edges before applying the rest.           │
│                          │ Here, we take that logic a step further by factoring the complete graph K8 into its 7     │
│                          │ perfect matchings and distributing them across three separate entangling blocks           │
│                          │ (Matchings 1-2, Matchings 3-4, Matchings 5-7).                                            │
│                          │ Between each block, we introduce parameter-efficient collective single-qubit rotations    │
│                          │ (alternating pairs of RY, RX, and RZ). This deeply interleaves trainable non-commuting    │
│                          │ operations with the fixed entanglement, giving the ansatz significantly greater           │
│                          │ expressivity while maintaining full permutation equivariance and remaining well within    │
│                          │ the parameter budget.                                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
