│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_cross_ry_rz_ansatz                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This design uses a brick-wall-inspired structure with two key entanglement patterns: a    │
│                          │ full ring of CZ gates (nearest-neighbor circular) and cross CZ connections (stride-4,     │
│                          │ connecting qubit q to q+4) for long-range entanglement. Single-qubit layers alternate RY  │
│                          │ and RZ rotations to provide full Bloch sphere coverage. The structure is: RY layer → RZ   │
│                          │ layer → Ring CZ → RY layer → Cross CZ → RZ layer. This gives 32 independent parameters    │
│                          │ per block. With p=2 repetitions and l=3 data re-uploads, the ansatz has 192 total ansatz  │
│                          │ parameters plus gain/bias. The ring topology ensures every qubit is entangled with its    │
│                          │ neighbors while the stride-4 cross connections create non-local correlations across the   │
│                          │ register, which is important for capturing feature interactions encoded by the IsingZZ    │
│                          │ feature map across different qubit pairs.                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
