│ patch_name               │ su2_readout_ladder                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This design retains the permutation-equivariant collective input mixer and                │
│                          │ depth-efficient K8 perfect-matching schedule that performed well in the prior candidates. │
│                          │ Its novel change concentrates additional expressivity at the measurement interface: the   │
│                          │ former single RX output rotation is replaced by a shared RX–RY–RX Euler ladder following  │
│                          │ the collective RZ layer. The three independently trained angles let each re-upload block  │
│                          │ expose multiple phase-coherence quadratures to the fixed mean-Z readout without adding    │
│                          │ two-qubit gates or breaking qubit-permutation symmetry. Parameter sharing keeps the block │
│                          │ at six parameters, while independent block copies preserve the temporal flexibility of    │
│                          │ data re-uploading.                                                                        │
