│ patch_name               │ trainable_matching_crz                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed, maximally entangling CZ network with trainable CRZ interactions,       │
│                          │ sharing one angle across each perfect matching. The seven matching-level parameters let   │
│                          │ Adam suppress redundant couplings or strengthen useful interaction classes while          │
│                          │ preserving complete K8 coverage and the disjoint-edge schedule. Because CRZ gates         │
│                          │ initialize near identity, they also provide a stable residual-like path early in          │
│                          │ training; the surrounding RX/RY mixers convert their learned phases into the mean-Z       │
│                          │ signal. Sharing within each matching regularizes the added expressivity compared with     │
│                          │ assigning a separate parameter to every edge.                                             │
