│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ three_stage_cz_dual_midmixers                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Split the 7 perfect matchings of K8 into three non-commuting stages separated by two      │
│                          │ mid-circuit RY+RX mixers instead of one. This creates three genuinely independent         │
│                          │ entangling layers (matchings 1-3, 4-5, 6-7) with non-commuting single-qubit rotations     │
│                          │ between them. The key insight is that consecutive CZ gates commute, so splitting them     │
│                          │ with parametrized rotations effectively increases the circuit's expressive power. This    │
│                          │ adds only 2 shared parameters per block (from 6 to 8), going from 38 to 50 total          │
│                          │ parameters, while significantly increasing the effective circuit depth and expressivity.  │
│                          │ The 3-2-2 split ensures a good balance of short-range (matchings 1-2), long-range         │
│                          │ (matching 3), cross (4-5), and diagonal (6-7) entanglement in each stage.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
