│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crz_matchings_with_mid_mixer                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This edit combines two improvements:                                                      │
│                          │ 1. The mid-circuit RY+RX mixer from the best-performing program (score 1.07), which       │
│                          │ breaks the commuting diagonal CZ sequence into two non-commuting interaction stages.      │
│                          │ 2. Replacing fixed CZ gates with parameterized CRZ gates, sharing one trainable parameter │
│                          │ per perfect matching (7 total). This lets the optimizer learn the ideal entanglement      │
│                          │ strength for each matching independently.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ CRZ gates are diagonal in the computational basis (like CZ), so consecutive matchings     │
│                          │ still commute—the mid-circuit mixer remains essential for breaking this commutativity.    │
│                          │ The seven perfect matchings cover all 28 K8 edges at minimum depth.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Parameters per block: 2 (input RY+RX) + 4 (CRZ matchings 1-4) + 2 (mid RY+RX) + 3 (CRZ    │
│                          │ matchings 5-7) + 2 (output RZ+RX) = 13.                                                   │
│                          │ Total: 13 × 6 blocks + 2 readout = 80 parameters.                                         │
