│ patch_name               │ brickwall_ring_cnot                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ A brick-wall entangling ansatz with ring topology. Key differences from the seed:         │
│                          │ 1. Two staggered CNOT layers per block (even pairs 0-1,2-3,4-5,6-7 then odd pairs         │
│                          │ 1-2,3-4,5-6,7-0) instead of a single linear CZ chain. This creates much faster            │
│                          │ entanglement spreading across all qubits.                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Ring closure (7→0 CNOT) ensures periodic boundary, preventing edge qubits from being   │
│                          │ under-entangled.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. CNOT instead of CZ gates - these create asymmetric entanglement (control vs target)    │
│                          │ which can be more expressive for classification.                                          │
│                          │ 4. Three rotation layers (RY+RZ, RY, RZ) interleaved with entangling layers, using all    │
│                          │ rotation axes for richer single-qubit expressibility.                                     │
│                          │ 5. Moderate parameter count (32 per block) balances expressibility against overfitting    │
│                          │ risk.                                                                                     │
